  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "architect",
      "heading": "Architect",
      "content": "**Filled by:** the Architect only — one subsection per entry, added as it works (not as a post-hoc summary) with `axiom_graph_add_section(parent_id=\"architect\", section_id=\"<short-tag-slug>\", heading=\"<short tag>\", content=...)`. The doc-scope hook allows each agent to add entries only under its own group.\n\n**Entry rule:** add one subsection per entry with `axiom_graph_add_section`. Entry ids are slugs with no dots. Omit `content` rather than passing `\"\"`. After two identical failures, change approach instead of retrying. The doc-scope hook refuses `axiom_graph_update_section` and `axiom_graph_patch_section` here, so an entry, once written, is never overwritten.\n\n**Entry format** (the subsection's heading is the short tag; its content is):\n```\n{one line: what felt off}\nContext: {raw paste — tool call, output, instruction fragment, error}\nWish: {optional — what would've made this easier}\n```\n\nFriction is what was hard or felt off, regardless of whether the agent deviated: an instruction that didn't fit, awkward tool output, a role constraint that pinched, upstream input that forced guessing, effort out of proportion to value. It is not a decision (`decisions`) or a deviation (`builder`). **Empty is fine** — honest emptiness beats invented friction."
    },
